From: SourbyCraft <noreply@sourbycraft>
Subject: [PATCH] downloader: do not trust HTTP 200, and verify before persisting

A slim jar cannot bootstrap in a clean directory. It fails with

    RuntimeException: All maven repo download attempts has been failed for library <id>!
      Suppressed: java.io.IOException: Downloaded library SHA-256 mismatch: <id>

for whichever library it reaches first.

Cause, established by probing the four repositories in Sourbyclip's list with
dev/iyanz/sourbycraft/sourbyapi/26.2-DEV/sourbyapi-26.2-DEV.jar, an artifact that is published
nowhere so every answer is necessarily a miss:

    maven.aliyun.com/repository/central        404   689 B
    repo.papermc.io/repository/maven-public    404   170 B
    repo.menthamc.org/repository/maven-public  200   995 B   <-- HTML, status 200
    repo.spongepowered.org/maven               404  1602 B

menthamc answers 200 with an HTML body for artifacts it does not have. A downloader that treats
200 as success writes that HTML into libraries/ under a .jar name and then fails its hash.

The libraries are not at fault. All 58 stripped entries resolve from at least one repository,
and zstd-jni hashes identically from Maven Central, aliyun and papermc, all three matching
libraries.list.

---

NOTE ON FORM. SourbyClip's sources are not in the SourbyCraft tree -- they live in the private
YanIanZ/SourbyClip repository, pinned by build-data/private-toolchain.lock.json. This patch was
reconstructed from the bytecode shipped inside SourbyCraft-slim.jar
(dev/iyanz/sourbyclip/downloader/Downloader.class, javap -c -p), so the structure and method
names are accurate but the surrounding source text is not verbatim. Apply by hand.

---

 src/main/java/dev/iyanz/sourbyclip/downloader/Downloader.java            | 38 ++++++++---
 src/main/java/dev/iyanz/sourbyclip/downloader/MavenDependencyResolver.java | 21 +++++-
 2 files changed

diff --git a/src/main/java/dev/iyanz/sourbyclip/downloader/Downloader.java b/src/main/java/dev/iyanz/sourbyclip/downloader/Downloader.java
--- a/src/main/java/dev/iyanz/sourbyclip/downloader/Downloader.java
+++ b/src/main/java/dev/iyanz/sourbyclip/downloader/Downloader.java
@@
-    private void deleteIfInvalid() throws IOException {
+    /**
+     * Renamed from deleteIfInvalid, which it never was: it deletes unconditionally. The old name
+     * implied a validity check that does not exist, and that reading is what made a deterministic
+     * failure look like a poisoned cache.
+     */
+    private void prepareOutput() throws IOException {
         if (!Files.isDirectory(this.outputDir)) {
             Files.createDirectories(this.outputDir);
         }
         Files.deleteIfExists(this.outputFile);
     }
+
+    /**
+     * Writes to a sibling temporary file, verifies it, and only then moves it into place.
+     *
+     * <p>Both call sites previously wrote straight to outputFile and validated afterwards, so
+     * between those two steps the final path held unverified bytes. A crash or a concurrent
+     * reader there sees a corrupt jar.</p>
+     */
+    private void writeVerified(final InputStream in, final String source) throws IOException {
+        final Path temporary = this.outputFile.resolveSibling(this.outputFile.getFileName() + ".part");
+        try {
+            Files.deleteIfExists(temporary);
+            try (final OutputStream out = Files.newOutputStream(temporary)) {
+                in.transferTo(out);
+            }
+            if (!Util.isFileValid(temporary, this.entry.hash())) {
+                throw new IOException(source + " library SHA-256 mismatch: " + this.entry.id());
+            }
+            Files.move(temporary, this.outputFile, StandardCopyOption.REPLACE_EXISTING);
+        } finally {
+            Files.deleteIfExists(temporary);
+        }
+    }
@@ bundled path
-        this.deleteIfInvalid();
-        this.write(stream);
-        if (!Util.isFileValid(this.outputFile, this.entry.hash())) {
-            throw new IOException("Bundled library SHA-256 mismatch: " + this.entry.id());
-        }
+        this.prepareOutput();
+        this.writeVerified(stream, "Bundled");
@@ download path
-        this.deleteIfInvalid();
-        final MavenDependencyResolver resolver = new MavenDependencyResolver(repositories, this.outputDir);
-        final MavenDependencyResolver.DownloadResult result = resolver.downloadTo(coordinate, this.outputFile);
-        if (!Util.isFileValid(this.outputFile, this.entry.hash())) {
-            throw new IOException("Downloaded library SHA-256 mismatch: " + this.entry.id());
-        }
+        this.prepareOutput();
+        final MavenDependencyResolver resolver = new MavenDependencyResolver(repositories, this.outputDir);
+        // Hand the expected hash down so the resolver can reject a repository's answer and try
+        // the next one, rather than accepting the first 200 and failing the whole attempt.
+        final MavenDependencyResolver.DownloadResult result =
+            resolver.downloadTo(coordinate, this.outputFile, this.entry.hash());
+        if (!result.success()) {
+            throw new IOException("Downloaded library SHA-256 mismatch: " + this.entry.id()
+                + " (tried " + result.attempted() + " repositories)");
+        }

diff --git a/src/main/java/dev/iyanz/sourbyclip/downloader/MavenDependencyResolver.java b/src/main/java/dev/iyanz/sourbyclip/downloader/MavenDependencyResolver.java
--- a/src/main/java/dev/iyanz/sourbyclip/downloader/MavenDependencyResolver.java
+++ b/src/main/java/dev/iyanz/sourbyclip/downloader/MavenDependencyResolver.java
@@
-    public DownloadResult downloadTo(final String coordinate, final Path target) {
+    public DownloadResult downloadTo(final String coordinate, final Path target,
+                                     final byte[] expectedHash) {
         for (final MavenRepository repository : this.repositories) {
-            // ... fetch; a 200 was taken as success
+            final Path candidate = this.fetch(repository, coordinate);
+            if (candidate == null) {
+                continue;
+            }
+            // A repository that answers 200 for an artifact it does not have -- menthamc serves
+            // an HTML page this way -- is a miss, not a hit. The status code is not the answer;
+            // the bytes are. Keep going rather than ending the attempt on the first 200.
+            if (expectedHash != null && !Util.isFileValid(candidate, expectedHash)) {
+                LOGGER.debug("{} returned content for {} that does not match its hash; trying the next repository",
+                    repository.name(), coordinate);
+                Files.deleteIfExists(candidate);
+                continue;
+            }
+            Files.move(candidate, target, StandardCopyOption.REPLACE_EXISTING);
+            return DownloadResult.success(repository);
         }
+        return DownloadResult.exhausted(this.repositories.size());
     }

--
Optional, and separable from the above: move repo.menthamc.org to the end of the repository
list, or drop it. That reduces how often the fallthrough is exercised but does not fix anything
by itself -- any mirror can answer 200 for a miss, and the resolver has to survive it.
